# Cloudflare Pages redirects.
#
# One hostname must win, or soilsums.com and www.soilsums.com serve the same
# pages at two addresses and split their own search ranking. Every canonical
# URL the site emits is on the apex, so www redirects to it.
#
# NOTE: this rule matches on the full URL, which Pages supports but which could
# not be verified from the machine that wrote it — this sandbox has no outbound
# access to Cloudflare. After the first deploy, check it:
#
#   curl -sI https://www.soilsums.com/tools/ | head -3
#
# Expect "301" and a Location on the apex. If instead you get a 200, delete
# this rule and do it at the zone level: Cloudflare dashboard -> your domain ->
# Rules -> Redirect Rules -> Create, matching hostname equals
# www.soilsums.com, with a dynamic redirect to
# concat("https://soilsums.com", http.request.uri.path) and status 301.
https://www.soilsums.com/*  https://soilsums.com/:splat  301
